[Music]  take a look at this it's the olympic  torch making its way to the beijing  competitions they're already underweight  they're winter games but the opening  ceremony is tomorrow you know it's been  a very long road to the chinese capital  and no one knows that better than the  athletes and other people who are  attending the games like  tada or jamie yukas she has navigated a  strict and complicated bubble that china  put in place just for this pandemic so  she documented her stressful journey and  she says stressful is the word all the  way from l.a to beijing  the skies over beijing sparkling all  week with rehearsals of friday's opening  ceremonies the athletes are settling  into the village but also in the  starting blocks anxiety and covet  concern everyone headed to the games had  to make serious preparations i just got  to the testing center which is just  about a half mile from the airport we  have to get a test at 96 hours out and  72 hours out so this is my first of two  before i leave in a couple of days  getting to the games required a series  of invasive tests and two weeks of  health monitoring using a chinese  created mobile app  [Laughter]  not nice for me  the negative test results and other  health data had to be uploaded and  reviewed by chinese organizers i've got  all my health declarations and paperwork  negative tests  i am headed to air france finally  approved we could board our flights but  flights that were restricted to carry  only olympic participants and that would  deliver us directly into the beijing  bubble during a layover in paris we  bumped into nicole savera from brazil's  skeleton team the last two months  specifically i think have been even  harder just trying to  just hide from covid we knew we  qualified but we couldn't really  celebrate final passage a 10 hour flight  complete with onboard temperature checks  thank you  we just got off the plane we were  temperature checked on the plane we're  now going up  starting our series of procedures  airport greeters in full ppe garp  escorted us through a final series of  health checks and throat swabs  fail here and it could mean days of  isolation after two days of travel in  the home stretch waiting for our luggage  we met the jamaican bobsled team who  agreed it was an olympian effort just to  get on chinese soil i think i have to do  five tests before i could even get on  the plane so it was always like a real  tense moment you never know what the  outcome was going to be but now that  we're actually here it's absolutely  amazing the airport testing has proven  to be where most of the positive cases  have been detected  american bobsledder alana myers-taylor  was among those positive she's now  isolated from her one-year-old son who  traveled alongside her desperately  waiting to clear protocol people are  well spaced out dr brian mccloskey  chairs the medical panel advising the  beijing organizers he says it's a  three-tiered approach the testing  process gradually takes people out of  the system so the pre-departure testing  the airport testing and then the daily  testing in the closed loop at each of  those levels people who might becoming  infectious are identified so the time we  get the closed loop it's a very low  level of people testing positive the  closed loop aka the bubble secure buses  to and from venues and hotels plexiglas  between workspaces and dining tables  robots cleaning the floors  and serving meals no contact with anyone  from mainland china and yes more testing  every day  we're almost to china many athletes  consider it a win just to get past the  battery of tests and pre-games  challenges posting with pride i don't  like the tests anymore than i did the  first time but  we feel super safe here  just with all everything involving covet  and  at least i'm super grateful that these  games can still happen it's on to the  competition while organizers hope their  own olympic prep pays off on keeping the  bubble clean  talk about an anxiety-inducing trip i  really lived in my own bubble before the  journey keeping my distance from many  family and friends or making them keep  their distance from me i didn't even go  to the grocery store you guys it was  like march 2020 all over again and now  that we're in this beijing bubble where  many of us are using burner phones there  are several questions about how the  chinese may use all of the health and  personal data that's being collected  nate  jamie thank you so much so jamie as  you're sitting there going through all  of these tests do you feel like they  have everything in control or as much as  they can  i have to tell you now that we're in the  ground on the ground in the beijing  bubble i feel so much better i think i  felt so anxious i was so upset i had my  therapist cynthia on speed dial while i  was in the united states because there's  such a hodgepodge of rules now that  you're here you have to follow the rule  book everyone wears a mask there's the  plexiglass between everything we're  getting tested every day there is a  little bit of calm each day as those  tests come back and they're negative  i i can't wait to see the coverage jamie  i can't get over those deep dive nasal  swabs that they do you know that that's  like back old school where it feels like  it's hitting your brain a do you feel it  was worth it clearly i think you do and  i i can't wait to see your coverage  well thank you uh i i always go into  these assignments thinking in 10 years  will i look back and be upset if i  didn't go and so i'm glad to be here  it's a historic games uh you know  there's been many lead up to to what's  going to happen here i'm also excited to  see uh lots of the athletes as they  compete we're already seeing uh you know  them trying to get into some of the  competition we've got curling luge going  on women's hockey is about to start uh  so it should be really good games to  watch yeah good jammie i'm glad that  you're finally settled we had lunch  right before you left so it's i'm glad  that you're doing so we're doing good  jamie yukas in beijing we'll be right  back

